   "path": "SCENE.md",
   "role": "instructions",
   "content": "# Bauhaus Build\n\nGeometric Bauhaus pieces tumble in, snap into a composition, then tumble away again.\n\nCategory: shapes. Length: 5 s. WebGL: no.\n\nUse when:\n- A geometric intro, title card or section transition should feel built, with shapes that tumble in and lock together.\n- A bold, flat, poster-like look is wanted.\n\nAvoid when:\n- You need a soft or photographic style.\n- The composition must stay on screen: the pieces tumble away again.\n\nVariables:\n- scale (number, 0.5-1.25): Scale, default 1\n- seed (number, 1-24): Seed, default 1\n- ink_color (color): Ink, default \"#1c1a17\"\n- accent_color (color): Accent, default \"#e4572e\"\n- secondary_color (color): Secondary, default \"#cbbc9f\"\n- tertiary_color (color): Tertiary, default \"#7e776b\"\n- speed (number, 0.25-3): Speed, default 1\n- loop (boolean): Loop, default false\n\nSource: https://github.com/Remocn/remocn. Licence: MIT. The scene file keeps the upstream notice.\n"
  },
